@obverse
1. a-na {d}UTU-ha-zi-ir qi₂-bi₂-ma
#tr.en.(o 2): Speak to Šamaš-hazir, thus (says) Hammurabi:
2. um-ma ha-am-mu-ra-bi-ma
3. A.ŠA₃ {d}EN.LIL₂-ša-du-u₂-šu
#tr.en.(o 5): (Concerning) the field of Enlil-šadûšu, which he held previously and is now under your control:
4. ša pa-na-nu-um iṣ-ba-tu-u₂-ma
5. i-na-an-na i-na qa₂-ti-ka i-ba-aš-šu-u₂
6. šum-ma A.ŠA₃-am šu-a-ti
#tr.en.(o 11): If you did not give out that field in its entirety, draw up, meadow by meadow, the 20 bur (i.e., 64.8 ha) field from his previous subsistence field, which are now irrigated and on which his oxen are working, and send it to me.
7. ga-me-er-šu a-na ṣi-tim la tu-še-ṣi
8. i-na A.ŠA₃ ŠUKU-šu pa-ni-tim
9. 20.0.0 GANA₂ A.ŠA₃-am ša# i-na-an-na im-ma-ak-ka-ru-ma
10. GU₄-HI.A-šu ši-ip-ra-am i-ip-pe₂-šu
11. u₂-ga-ri-ša-am šu-uṭ-ra-am-ma
12. šu-bi-lam
13. šum#-ma A.ŠA₃ {d}EN.LIL₂-ša-du-u₂-šu ga-me-er-šu
#tr.en.(r 5): If you have given out the field of Enlil-šadûšu in its entirety, draw up, meadow by meadow, the 20 bur field among the irrigated field(s), which are under your control, and send it to me.
@bottom
1. a-na ṣi-i-tim tu-uš-te-ṣi
@reverse
1. i-na A.ŠA₃-im ma-ak-ri-im
2. ša i-na qa₂-ti-ka i-ba-aš-šu-u₂
3. 20.0.0 GANA₂ A.ŠA₃-am u₂-ga-ri-ša-am
4. šu-uṭ-ra-am
5. šu-bi-lam-ma
6. a-na pi₂-i tup-pi-ka ša tu-ša-ab-ba-lam
#tr.en.(r 8): A sealed document will be issued according to the wording of your tablet that you send to me, and you will give him the field. 
7. ka-ni-kum ik-ka-an-na-ak-kum-ma
8. A.ŠA₃-am ta-na-ad-di-iš-šum
$ end of side